      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": "2",
          "section": "2.1 Material preparation",
          "quote": "Alloys with a standard composition of (ZrTiNb)100-xTax (at%, x = 0, 5, 10, and 15) were fabricated via arc melting using pure metals of Zr, Ti, Nb, and Ta (> 99.95 wt%) and labeled as Ta0, Ta5, Ta10, and Ta15 RHEAs. The Zr-Ti and Nb-Ta intermediate alloys were separately prepared to ensure uniform melting, after which they were melted together and consolidated into button ingots. The button ingots were re-melted and flipped at least seven times to ensure their chemical homogeneity under the protection of a high-purity argon atmosphere, and then cast into a water-cooled copper mold (8 × 12 × 40 mm3).",
          "table": null,
